A||||5||Call||Question on a 1985 Fiero GT That Wont Start||||5||
Z||000000||Call||01-17-2000||12:52 PM||||I found a 1985 Fiero GT here at a dealer that has some side body damage and the engine wont start. What do you guys think could be wrong with the engine? Could it be an ignition problem or another problem that is cheap to fix?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||01-17-2000||12:57 PM||||Call, I think you'll need more info. "Won't start" could be anything from a low battery to a ruined engine with a LOT of things in between.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Call||01-17-2000||01:01 PM||||What are some quick things i could check at the dealer by looking at it?||||reg||5
Z||000003||Phil||01-17-2000||01:34 PM||||Is this the dealer that wants $2500 ? If there were an easy fix to the motor he would have done it. I say again look elsewhere||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||01-17-2000||01:44 PM||||Like I said it could be a lot of things. Most likely you won't be able to find out until it's yours (too late). I would assume the engine is totally gone (unless they are willing to get it started for you) and make an offer accordingly. <P>BTW, saw your post in the other section. $2500 is about all it's worth in average condition running and not wrecked. Don't offer money hoping for the "best case" of what is wrong or you will probably get burned. Assume the worst!!!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Call||01-17-2000||01:44 PM||||Is the one you looked at located at a Arrow Ford? If so that is the one. I am going to go ahead and go look at anyway (I need to make sure i will fit in a Fiero, when i get one this will be my first car <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)when i go look at it I will take a good look at it and ask alot of questions. They said that they would come down and im going to take some printouts of some 85' GTs and some 86 GTs I found on the net for $900-$1900 that run good and are in good condition. Hopefully this will force them to give me a really good deal on the car maybe like $300-$500 for the whole thing. At that peice I could have the engine rebuilt for like $1000 and the body damage isn't a big deal as long as it hasn't bent the frame since in a few months it will be a Ferrari 308.<BR>||||reg||5
